          "tz": -300
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Patrick Farrell",
          "email": "patrick@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-10-11 16:00:01.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-17601 tests: don't check striped dir MDTs in sanity 413a/b",
        "message": "LU-17601 tests: don't check striped dir MDTs in sanity 413a/b\n\nsanity test_413a and test_413b check that space-balanced mkdir\ndoes not spread 240/N directories of N stripes evenly over the\nMDTs.  The MDT of each directory is picked at random by weight,\nand with the fullest MDT at about 45% of the weight of the\nothers, 80 directories of 3 stripes are spread evenly by chance\nin about 0.13% of runs, which matches the rate the tests fail\nat in CI, always for stripe_count=3.\n\nThe client picks the MDT the same way whatever the stripe count,\nso only check it for the 240 plain directories, and rely on the\ncheck of the stripes for striped directories.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial mdtcount=4 mdscount=2 testlist=sanity env=ONLY=413,ONLY_REPEAT=5\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I14e94cee2cda355d383251481d1f05ff4035b38d\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
